title: Clara Zetkin
is-pinned-card: true
tags: advisor
view-if: adv_show_zetkin = 1
new-page: true

= Clara Zetkin

The grand old woman of the socialist women's movement, friend of Luxemburg and of Lenin alike. She founded International Women's Day, edits the party's women's paper, and every current in the party still listens to her.

[? if kpd_seats > 0 : She sits in the Reichstag for the party. ?]

- @mediate
- @lenin
- @root: Return to main

@mediate
title: Mediate Between the Currents
subtitle: The angriest current is heard out.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 5;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
var low = null;
for (var f of Q.factions) {
    if (!Q[f + '_gone'] && (low === null || Q[f + '_satisfaction'] < Q[low + '_satisfaction'])) {
        low = f;
    }
}
if (low) {
    Q[low + '_satisfaction'] += 10;
}
Q.unity += 3;
!}

Zetkin spends long evenings with the angriest comrades. She scolds them and then defends them, and they leave calmer than they came.

@lenin
title: Write to Lenin
subtitle: She has known him for twenty years. He will read it himself.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?][? if comintern_member = 0 : We are not in the International. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and comintern_member = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 6;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
RG.ecci('lenin', 10);
Q.independence += 2;
!}

Zetkin writes to Lenin in longhand, eleven pages, about what the German party needs and what it does not need from Moscow. An answer comes within the month, short and friendly.
